IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-cpc-interface`
IMPORT `ea-types`
IMPORT `ea-statements`

-- Tests for ea-statements.l4 (Evidence Act 1893, ss 17 to 23, 31, 32, 32A, 32B, 32C, 33).
-- Expected values are read off the Act's text and illustrations.  Generated by generators/ea_tests_1.py.

`criminal proceedings with the Code's notice conditions met` MEANS `Code Conclusions` WITH
    `the notice requirements and other conditions prescribed under section 428 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 are complied with` IS TRUE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible by virtue of section 265 or 266 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS FALSE
`criminal proceedings without the Code's notice conditions met` MEANS `Code Conclusions` WITH
    `the notice requirements and other conditions prescribed under section 428 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 are complied with` IS FALSE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible by virtue of section 265 or 266 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS FALSE

§ `17 to 20. Admissions and confessions`

`party statement suggesting an inference` MEANS `Admission Facts` WITH
    `the statement is oral or documentary` IS TRUE
    `the statement suggests an inference as to a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS TRUE
    `the maker is a person accused of an offence` IS FALSE
    `the statement states or suggests the inference that the maker committed that offence` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a party to the proceeding` IS TRUE
    `the maker is an agent of a party whom the court regards in the circumstances as expressly or impliedly authorised by the party to make the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a party suing or sued in a representative character` IS FALSE
    `the maker held that representative character when making the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker has a proprietary or pecuniary interest in the subject matter of the proceeding and made the statement in that character` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a person from whom a party to the suit derived the party's interest in the subject matter` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made during the continuance of the maker's interest` IS FALSE
    `the maker's position or liability must be proved as against a party to the suit` IS FALSE
    `the statement would be relevant as against the maker in relation to the position or liability in a suit brought by or against the maker` IS FALSE
    `the maker occupied the position or was subject to the liability when making the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a person to whom a party to the suit has expressly referred for information in reference to the matter in dispute` IS FALSE
    `the admission is sought to be proved against the maker or the maker's representative in interest` IS FALSE
    `the admission is sought to be proved by or on behalf of the maker or the maker's representative in interest` IS FALSE
    `the admission is of such a nature that, if the maker were dead, it would be relevant between third persons under section 32` IS FALSE
    `the admission is a statement of a state of mind or body, relevant or in issue, made at or about the time it existed and accompanied by conduct rendering its falsehood improbable` IS FALSE
    `the admission is relevant otherwise than as an admission` IS FALSE
    `the admission is an oral admission as to the contents of a document` IS FALSE
    `the party proposing to prove it shows that the party is entitled to give secondary evidence of the contents of the document` IS FALSE
    `the genuineness of a document produced is in question` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are civil proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the admission was made upon an express condition that evidence of it is not to be given` IS FALSE
    `the admission was made upon circumstances from which the court can infer that the parties agreed together that evidence of it should not be given` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a matter that an advocate or solicitor may be compelled to give evidence of under section 128` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a matter that a legal counsel in an entity may be compelled to give evidence of under section 128A` IS FALSE

