§ `32(1). Statements by persons who need not be called, one case for each paragraph`

`s32(1)(a) ill a the dying statement` MEANS `Hearsay Facts` WITH
    `the statement is of a relevant fact` IS TRUE
    `the statement was made by a person, whether orally, in a document or otherwise` IS TRUE
    `the statement is a protest, greeting or other verbal utterance and the relevant fact is one the utterance implies` IS FALSE
    `the statement is made by a person as to the cause of that person's death, or as to a circumstance of the transaction that resulted in that person's death` IS TRUE
    `the cause of that person's death comes into question` IS TRUE
    `the statement was made by a person in the ordinary course of a trade, business, profession or other occupation` IS FALSE
    `the statement is made in a document that is, or forms part of, a record compiled by a person acting in the ordinary course of a trade, business, profession or other occupation on information supplied by other persons` IS FALSE
    `the statement is against the pecuniary or proprietary interest of the person making it` IS FALSE
    `the statement, if true, would expose or would have exposed the maker to a criminal prosecution or to a suit for damages` IS FALSE
    `the statement gives the opinion of the maker as to the existence of a public right or custom or a matter of public or general interest` IS FALSE
    `the maker would have been likely to be aware of the existence of that right, custom or matter if it existed` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made before any controversy as to that right, custom or matter had arisen` IS FALSE
    `the statement relates to the existence of a relationship by blood, marriage or adoption between persons as to whose relationship the maker had special means of knowledge` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made before the question in dispute was raised` IS FALSE
    `the statement relates to the existence of a relationship by blood, marriage or adoption between deceased persons and is made in a will or deed relating to the affairs of their family, in a family pedigree, or upon a tombstone, family portrait or other thing on which such statements are usually made` IS FALSE
    `the statement is contained in a deed or other document relating to a transaction mentioned in section 13(a)` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made by a number of persons and expressed feelings or impressions on their part relevant to the matter in question` IS FALSE
    `the maker is compellable to give evidence on behalf of the party desiring to give the statement in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the maker attends or is brought before the court` IS FALSE
    `the maker refuses to be sworn or affirmed` IS FALSE
    `the maker is sworn or affirmed but refuses to give any evidence` IS FALSE
    `the maker is dead` IS FALSE
    `the maker is unfit because of a bodily or mental condition to attend as a witness` IS FALSE
    `despite reasonable efforts to locate the maker, the maker cannot be found, whether within or outside Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the maker is outside Singapore and it is not practicable to secure the maker's attendance` IS FALSE
    `the maker is competent but not compellable to give evidence on behalf of the party desiring to give the statement in evidence, and refuses to do so` IS FALSE
    `the parties to the proceedings agree that for the purpose of those proceedings the statement may be given in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the oral statement was put by another person, at the maker's request, into writing at the time or reasonably soon afterwards` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the statement as relevant` IS FALSE
    `the kind of proceedings` IS `criminal proceedings`
    `the notice requirements and other conditions prescribed in the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are complied with` IS FALSE
    `the statement is to be given in evidence on the prosecution's behalf` IS FALSE
    `when the agreement was made the accused or a co-accused was represented by an advocate` IS FALSE
    `the agreement was made during proceedings before an examining Magistrate conducting a committal hearing under Division 2 of Part 10 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as in force immediately before 17 September 2018` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are before the General Division of the High Court or arise out of proceedings before it` IS FALSE

