`s32C absent maker, evidence admissible had the maker been called` MEANS `Credibility of Absent Maker Facts` WITH
    `the statement is given in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS TRUE
    `the maker of the statement is not called as a witness in the proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the evidence would have been admissible to undermine or support the maker's credibility had the maker been called` IS TRUE
    `the matter could have been put to the maker in cross-examination for the purpose of undermining credibility, and evidence of it could not have been adduced by the cross-examining party if the maker had denied it` IS FALSE
    `the court gives permission for evidence of that matter` IS FALSE
    `the evidence tends to prove that the maker made, before or after the statement, another statement inconsistent with it` IS FALSE

`s32C maker called as a witness` MEANS `Credibility of Absent Maker Facts` WITH
    `the statement is given in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS TRUE
    `the maker of the statement is not called as a witness in the proceedings` IS FALSE
