`s32C(2) inconsistent statement` MEANS `Credibility of Absent Maker Facts` WITH
    `the statement is given in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS TRUE
    `the maker of the statement is not called as a witness in the proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the evidence would have been admissible to undermine or support the maker's credibility had the maker been called` IS FALSE
    `the matter could have been put to the maker in cross-examination for the purpose of undermining credibility, and evidence of it could not have been adduced by the cross-examining party if the maker had denied it` IS FALSE
    `the court gives permission for evidence of that matter` IS FALSE
    `the evidence tends to prove that the maker made, before or after the statement, another statement inconsistent with it` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `evidence going to the credibility of the absent maker is admissible under section 32C(1)(a)` `s32C absent maker, evidence admissible had the maker been called`

#ASSERT NOT `evidence going to the credibility of the absent maker is admissible under section 32C(1)(a)` `s32C maker called as a witness`

#ASSERT `evidence going to the credibility of the absent maker is admissible under section 32C(1)(b)` `s32C(1)(b) with permission`

#ASSERT NOT `evidence going to the credibility of the absent maker is admissible under section 32C(1)(b)` `s32C(1)(b) without permission`

#ASSERT `evidence of an inconsistent statement by the absent maker is admissible under section 32C(2)` `s32C(2) inconsistent statement`

§ `33. Evidence given in an earlier proceeding`

`s33 witness dead, same parties` MEANS `Former Testimony Facts` WITH
    `the evidence was given by a witness in a judicial proceeding or before a person authorised by law to take it` IS TRUE
    `the witness is dead` IS TRUE
    `the witness cannot be found` IS FALSE
    `the witness is incapable of giving evidence` IS FALSE
    `the witness is kept out of the way by the adverse party` IS FALSE
    `the court considers that the witness's presence cannot be obtained without an amount of delay or expense that is unreasonable in the circumstances` IS FALSE
    `the proceeding was between the same parties or their representatives in interest` IS TRUE
    `the earlier proceeding was a criminal trial or inquiry and the later proceeding is between the same prosecutor and accused` IS FALSE
    `the adverse party in the first proceeding had the right and opportunity to cross-examine` IS TRUE
    `the questions in issue were substantially the same in the first as in the second proceeding` IS TRUE

